    "md5": "5b612033de49c6d4b7e82ce7411d1d84",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1896,
    "chunk_text": "This is a different kind of guidebook, the 1st guidebook created for the Indian market by Indians. It is a well established opinion that Sri Lanka\u2019s travel and tourism industry is reactive and derivative, never path breaking and never pro-active. We must commend Jetwing and  Ceylon Roots for breaking the pattern. They have been proactive, they have looked ahead and they have taken the initiative. Instead of waiting for things to happen, they have gone to the roots of the market and tried to shape it; instead of being bystanders, they have attempted to become participants and stakeholders.\n\nTravel is a form of conversation, an interaction with places, buildings, peoples, history, philosophy, food, music and art. Guided and supported by Jetwing and Ceylon Roots, the authors have travelled widely and deeply. They have experienced and they have studied. But what is important is that they have listened, they have learned and they have understood.\n\nGoing well beyond the usual tourist sights and sounds, Dr Vipin and Vidushi have experienced many different aspects of life on the island and immersed themselves in its culture and environment. They have seen things and done things which would normally take several months. This has been made possible by careful planning and meticulous organization on the part of  Ceylon Roots and elegant hospitality by Jetwing. This speaker still remembers the curated, crafted, dinners which enriched our interaction in Kandy and made such a spectacular statement of style.\n\nThis journey has produced a narrative which is well written and accessible. It is detailed and informed. The authors have taken the time and the trouble to think, read and study. The end result is a much deeper, more knowledgeable experience of Sri Lanka in all its many forms and faces. It is enriched by feeling and sensitivity, driven by the desire to know and to absorb."
  },
