    "chunk_text": "Democrats sweep elections in New York, New Jersey, Virginia and California\n\nThe entirety of the Epstein files likely to be released next week\n\nThe deep blue state of New York, elected as the mayor of its greatest city, New York City, the financial capital of the world, its Democratic candidate. No surprise there. The anomaly was that the choice was 34-year-old, Ugandan-born, first-generation immigrant, Zohran Mamdani, who was espousing the progressive movement started by President Franklin. D. Roosevelt in 1945.\n\nFDR\u2019s New Deal dealt with the Great Depression of the early 1930s, and continued until the 1980s, which had by then included social security, unemployment and disability insurance and provision of a just social safety net, with equitable taxation programs.\n\nThe Republican western film actor/president, Ronald Reagan, arguably the first true conservative president since WWII, went on to dismantle a thriving middle class, by embracing the theory of \u201csupply side economics\u201d aka \u201ctrickle-down economics\u201d.\n\nHe changed the demographic composition of the Republican Party of today: lower taxes, fewer corporate regulations against pollution of the environment and a strong military.\n\nIt\u2019s a pity that Reagan decided to quit his Hollywood job and run for the presidency. Hollywood\u2019s gain was the nation\u2019s loss.\n\nAfter Reagan\u2019s presidential terms, words like \u201cliberal\u201d, \u201cprogressive\u201d and the more recent \u201cwoke\u201d were considered to be insulting epithets. These words represent the economic policies of 29 of the 30 world\u2019s developed nations which follow the progressive ideology of socialist democracy."
