    "chunk_text": "After Reagan\u2019s presidential terms, words like \u201cliberal\u201d, \u201cprogressive\u201d and the more recent \u201cwoke\u201d were considered to be insulting epithets. These words represent the economic policies of 29 of the 30 world\u2019s developed nations which follow the progressive ideology of socialist democracy.\n\nThe Sanders movement is gaining in popularity, and will be the moving force behind the current Democratic Party, whose performance during the past eight years has been nothing short of abysmal, with its leadership behaving like moderate members of the Republican Party.\n\nThe first major elections during the second Trump administration were held on November 4, in New York City, Virginia, New Jersey and California. They were supposed to be close, a referendum on Trump\u2019s second term performance. All four elections proved to be a big night for the Democrats, with moderates Mikie Sherill and Abigail Spanberger becoming governors of New Jersey and Virginia, respectively. California said YES to Proposition 50, which will allow state legislators to redistrict the state before the midterms, in an effort to stop Trump led \u201cgerrymandering\u201d in other Republican states.\n\nThe Democrats, with the wind at its back, with the electorate generally disgruntled with Trump\u2019s blatant lies about his performance, as shown by the seven-million strong protest in over 250 cities against Trump two weeks ago. The Democrats had the ideal opportunity of showing the American electorate that the Republican administration was unable to govern, with the continuance of the 40+ day of the government shutdown, even with control of both Houses of Congress and the presidency."
