    "chunk_size_bytes": 1874,
    "chunk_text": "This was a couple of days after The Daily Telegraph published details of a leaked internal memo arguing that a BBC Panorama documentary had juxtaposed comments by Mr Trump in a way that made it appear that he had explicitly encouraged the attack on Jan 6, 2021 Mr Davie admitted the BBC was not a perfect organization and had to be open, transparent and accountable. \u201cOverall the BBC has been delivering well but the current debate around BBC News has understandably contributed to my decision. As director general I have to take ultimate responsibility.\u201d Ms Turness echoed this by admitting she had to take responsibility for any mistakes made down the line below her.\n\nis to retire after 39 years in the US House of Representatives as after a distinguished career as San Francisco\u2019s representative and the only woman to be Speaker of the House. \u201cShe wielded immense power and became a Democratic icon, while she was demonized by conservatives.\u201d\n\nShe and Donald Trump had a running battle. He called her names like Crazy Nancy and accused her of being \u201ccorrupt, evil and did only bad things for America.\u201d She replied with \u201cvile creature.\u201d\n\nShe married Paul Pelosi after being a co-student at Georgetown University and spent many years as a housewife bringing up their five children. Then she came into politics and never looked back, doing much good such as pushing Obamacare through successful legislation; steps to reduce climate change; improve infrastructure. Earlier on she moved very forcibly for the country to help AIDS patients, particularly teenagers, financially and otherwise.\n\nDuring the 2021 assault on the Capitol her room was targeted and much destruction caused. In October, for political reasons, Paul Pelosi was savagely attacked and seriously injured. She was by his side for months during his recovery and convalescence. He is now OK."
