    "chunk_text": "People\u2019s Bank becomes first state bank to secure Corporate Finance Advisor Licence\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank has made history by becoming the first State Bank in Sri Lanka to be granted the Corporate Finance Advisor Licence by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka, reaffirming its leadership in financial innovation and excellence.\n\nThis milestone further strengthens the mandate of the People\u2019s Bank Investment Banking Unit (PBIBU) \u2014 a pioneering arm of the Bank established to enhance its presence in Sri Lanka\u2019s capital markets and deliver cutting-edge financing solutions to clients across sectors.\n\nSince its inception, PBIBU has been at the forefront of Sri Lanka\u2019s capital market development, consistently setting industry benchmarks through innovative transactions and trusted advisory services.\n\nPBIBU has successfully managed and placed several milestone issuances over the years, each representing a significant contribution to the advancement of Sri Lanka\u2019s capital market. The below transactions not only demonstrate PBIBU\u2019s strong structuring and placement capabilities but also highlight its pivotal role in facilitating large-scale corporate and state-sector funding initiatives:\n\n2013 \u2013 Inaugural listed debenture of HDFC Bank of Sri Lanka, amounting to Rs. 2,000 million.\n\n2014 \u2013 Listed debenture issuance for Kotagala Plantations PLC, amounting to Rs. 1,000 million.\n\n2015 \u2013Equity issuance of People\u2019s Insurance PLC, amounting to Rs. 750 million.\n\n2020 \u2013BASEL III\u2013compliant, Tier 2, unlisted, rated debenture issued by People\u2019s Bank, amounting to Rs. 20,000 million.\n\n2021 \u2013 The pioneering listed debenture issue for the Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB), amounting to Rs. 20,000 million.\n\n2021 \u2013Successfully placed listed debenture issue for LOLC Holdings PLC, amounting to Rs. 10,000 million.\n\n2021 \u2013 Listed, Rated, Senior debentures of People\u2019s Leasing & Finance PLC, amounting to Rs. 10,000 million."
