    "md5": "82cd1be742b3dad76fd45459d188294e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1114,
    "chunk_text": "This minor adjustment would make the tax structure cleaner and more coherent, without adding any real burden on businesses or consumers.\n\nThe SSCL, at 2%, should be limited only to non-VAT-registered persons \u2014 mainly traders who buy and sell, and small-scale suppliers whose turnover is below the VAT threshold.\n\nThese proposals are not radical reforms \u2014 they are restorations of balance and common sense.\n\nFor too long, our tax system has been weighed down by duplication, inconsistency, and policy drift. By clearly separating VAT and SSCL, and by returning VAT to its original focus on value addition, Sri Lanka can create a more rational, transparent, and growth-friendly tax framework.\n\nA fair tax system is not only about collecting revenue; it\u2019s about building confidence \u2014 among taxpayers, investors, and the public at large. Implementing these measures will help rebuild that confidence and lay the foundation for a more stable and equitable fiscal future.\n\n(The author is a Retired Deputy Commissioner General of the Inland Revenue Department and could be reached via email at [email\u00a0protected])"
