    "chunk_text": "Vice Chancellor of the University of Colombo, Professor Indika Mahesh Karunathilake, described the initiative as a \u201chistoric collaboration\u201d that demonstrates the value of interdisciplinary science and institutional partnerships.\n\nReflecting on the COVID-19 pandemic, Prof. Karunathilake said the experience underlined the importance of scientific networks and evidence-based decision-making. \u201cDuring the pandemic, strong collaboration between academia and health authorities helped shape national protocols. These investments in diagnostics and training bring tangible returns \u2014 in public health and economic continuity alike, he said.\n\nProfessor Andreas Nitsche of the Robert Koch Institute outlined the achievements and next steps of the project, which has been active in Sri Lanka since 2017 under Germany\u2019s global health framework.\n\nWorldwide Week of Italian Cuisine returns to Colombo for 10th edition\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
