    "language": "en",
    "md5": "4a63f3f61002654f819a66f628246606",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1930,
    "chunk_text": "However every promise carries pitfalls. The Budget\u2019s success depends on implementation choices that are less glamorous than speeches or headline numbers. Equity shortfall. Centralised projects can paradoxically widen gaps if procurement, roll-out and teacher training focus on better connected urban schools. The DCS data showing stark urban-rural differences in computer literacy underline this risk: without explicit ring-fenced funding for remote and estate schools, the poorest children may be left further behind.\n\nTeacher capacity bottleneck: Technology without pedagogy is decoration. Large numbers of teachers will need sustained professional development, not one-off workshops, to make technology an integrated part of teaching, and that requires funding for mentoring, follow-ups and incentives.\n\nProcurement and governance vulnerabilities: Big IT projects attract vendor complexity and political risk. Transparent procurement, open dashboards and independent audits are essential to prevent delays, cost overruns and misuse.\n\nMismatch between mobile use and PC skills: A \u201cmobile-first\u201d population means many citizens are digitally active, but not necessarily computer-literate. Policies must deliberately scaffold mobile skills into formal computer competence, otherwise young people will remain employable mainly for low-value informal activities.\n\nPublish a time-bound target such as \u201craise national computer literacy from 35.9% to X% by 2028,\u201d broken down by province and sector, and attach KPIs for device uptime, teacher training completion rates and student learning outcomes. Targets make Ministries accountable and let donors and civil society measure progress.\n\nDedicate a visible tranche of the digital allocation to rural/estate connectivity, community learning centres and device maintenance. These ring-fenced sums should be conditional on provincial implementation plans and monitored centrally."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-17-islandlk-45143cc3",
