    "chunk_size_bytes": 1521,
    "chunk_text": "Chairs and tables \u2026 to the fore!\n\nAn ungainly sight seems to have cropped up in the entertainment scene with certain artistes using chairs, and also tables, to perform (sing and dance) at public events.\n\nOne must remember that chairs are for sitting and tables are for guests to have their meals.\n\nThe question being asked by many is whether these chairs and tables are cleaned, after improper use, so that the guests present can feel comfortable using them?\n\nThere should be a limit to what singers can do to project themselves while performing.\n\nIt\u2019s certainly jarring to see performers using furniture in ways it is not intended for, especially when it\u2019s a public event.\n\nAt Oktoberfest, however, dancing on benches (not chairs) is a common sight and part of the festive atmosphere; dancing, and singing along to traditional German folk songs, and having a blast, but dancing on tables is not allowed.\n\nI\u2019m told that security guards are quick to intervene if someone climbs on a table, as it poses a risk of knocking over drinks or hurting someone.\n\nIf this is not nipped in the bud, we may even see artistes walking on tables, encouraging those seated at the table, to sing along with them!\n\nWhere we stand, how Budget 2026 funds progress and what next\n\nBlue Economy: What Sri Lanka can learn from Indian initiatives\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
