    "md5": "7b8c3a85dbf535681aef085ed456061c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1526,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka launches GEW 2025 with national unity and entrepreneurial spirit\n\nSri Lanka last week officially launched Global Entrepreneurship Week (GEW) 2025 under the inspiring theme \u2018Together We Build,\u2019 commencing a nationwide celebration of innovation, inclusion, and economic empowerment.\n\nGlobal Entrepreneurship Week (GEW) is an annual worldwide movement celebrating innovators and entrepreneurs, promoting creativity, collaboration, and economic growth. This year, Sri Lanka continues the country\u2019s engagement as part of the global network, with ICTA once again serving as the National Host Organisation.\n\n\u2018Together We Build\u2019 champions the initiative to unite Sri Lanka\u2019s entrepreneurial ecosystem, empower communities, and drive sustainable growth through innovation. GEW 2025 unfolds countrywide, and Sri Lanka is poised to amplify its voice on the global stage, advocating creativity, resilience, and collaboration.\n\nThe launch was held at Temple Trees on 14 November\u00a0 under the distinguished patronage of Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya. The event renewed Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to cultivate entrepreneurship as a catalyst for national development.\n\nSupporting the entrepreneurial spirit around the nation, parallel launch events were simultaneously held throughout all nine provinces, within the first two hours of the Colombo ceremony, including the Prime Minister\u2019s keynote address, live streamed to all provincial venues, guaranteeing inclusive participation from every corner of Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
