    "language": "en",
    "md5": "782ba34c33a2ef7ee5ea323b16cee081",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1640,
    "chunk_text": "Supporting the entrepreneurial spirit around the nation, parallel launch events were simultaneously held throughout all nine provinces, within the first two hours of the Colombo ceremony, including the Prime Minister\u2019s keynote address, live streamed to all provincial venues, guaranteeing inclusive participation from every corner of Sri Lanka.\n\nChief Adviser to the President on Digital Economy and ICTA Chairman Dr. Hans Wijayasuriya,\n\ndelivered the welcome address. GEN Global Representative Suresh de Mel, also spoke.\n\nA special segment titled, \u2018Empowering the Future: The Gig and Digital Economy\u2019 showcased impactful private sector partnerships and financial empowerment initiatives for startups and SMEs. The panel discussion \u2018The 2035 Playbook: How Sri Lanka Builds Its Next Era of Entrepreneurs\u2019 focused on partnerships, innovation, and startup growth.\n\nA thematic video screening captured the energy of GEW 2025 and previewed district-level activities, were followed by closing remarks, a media briefing, and networking.\n\nThe GEW Sri Lanka 2025 launch extended from ceremonial to an activated movement. It heralded a nationwide mobilisation. This year, the initiative is targeting rolling out 900 events throughout the country in all 25 districts. The campaign aims to onboard 250 partners and engage over 30,000 participants countrywide, creating an unprecedented entrepreneurial engagement in Sri Lanka.\n\nTo achieve these ambitious targets, national partners joining the campaign include Vidatha, NEDA, SED, IDB, NYC, and NYSC. Notable, many other partners have already joined the movement demonstrating strong support."
