    "chunk_size_bytes": 1891,
    "chunk_text": "David Pieris Logistics acquires Logicare in Rs. 1.3 b deal from Ceylon Tea Brokers\n\nFrom left: Capital Alliance Partners CEO Nishok Goonasekera, DPL Executive Director Indika De Silva, Non-Executive Director Manjula De Alwis, David Pieris Motor Company Director Dhanika de Silva, Ceylon Tea Brokers Director Chrishantha Perera, Chairman Niraj De Mel, David Pieris Group Chairman and Managing Director Rohana Dissanayake, Ceylon Tea Brokers Managing Director Waruna De Silva, DPL Managing Director and CEO Kalum Katipearachchi, David Pieris Holdings Director Ashan Nissanka, and DPL Non-Executive Director Mavali Weerasinghe\n\nD.P. Logistics Ltd. (DPL), a member of the David Pieris Group of Companies, has entered into a Share Sale and Purchase Agreement for the acquisition of Logicare Ltd. from Ceylon Tea Brokers PLC for an enterprise value of Rs. 1.3 billion. The transaction includes a payment of Rs. 635.3 million to Ceylon Tea Brokers PLC as purchase consideration and taking over bank and other related party borrowings, making up the balance investment.\n\nThe Share Sale and Purchase Agreement, executed on 30 October, covers the acquisition of 100% of the issued shares in Logicare Ltd., with completion to take place upon the fulfilment of specified conditions.\n\nDPL currently ranks among the top ten companies in warehousing and 3PL operations and holds one of the largest container fleets amongst the logistics companies in the country. Despite operating in a highly fragmented freight forwarding market, DPL continues to capture a growing share, reinforcing its reputation as one of the very few local companies with expertise across all logistics disciplines.\n\nDavid Pieris Group also acquired in 2022, Pulsar Shipping Agencies Ltd., the shipping arm of Expolanka Holdings PLC to expand its Logistics & Shipping Cluster into ship agency, husbandry services and marine logistics."
  },
