    "md5": "f4595f860f9356dcc397c6b6767aa1c5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1390,
    "chunk_text": "Gahanu Eka Mittata \u2013 So Radical Without Money\n\nThe Committee Stage of the Ministry of Women & Child Affairs will be up for debate at some point. 2025 (Estimate / Appropriation Act, First Schedule) \u2014 Ministry of Women & Child Affairs: Recurrent LKR 15,234,000,000 + Capital LKR 842,000,000 \u2192 Total LKR 16,076,000,000. Parliament of Sri Lanka\n\n* 2026 (Estimate / First Schedule) \u2014 Ministry of Women & Child Affairs: Recurrent LKR 15,800,000,000 + Capital LKR 600,000,000 \u2192 Total LKR 16,400,000,000. Parliament of Sri Lanka\n\nThe ministry totals above are part of the First Schedule (the consolidated list of ministry recurrent + capital allocations). Using the First-Schedule totals:\n\n* Total First-Schedule government spending (2025) = Recurrent LKR 2,898,098,018,000 + Capital LKR 1,320,150,000,000 = LKR 4,218,248,018,000. Parliament of Sri Lanka\n\nMinistry of Women (LKR 16,076,000,000) as a share of this = 0.381% (\u2248 0.38%). (Calculation shown below.) Parliament of Sri Lanka\n\n* Total First-Schedule government spending (2026) = Recurrent LKR 3,028,753,468,000 + Capital LKR 1,405,603,000,000 = LKR 4,434,356,468,000. Parliament of Sri Lanka\n\nMinistry of Women (LKR 16,400,000,000) as a share of this = 0.370% (\u2248 0.37%). Parliament of Sri Lanka\n\nThe Exact calculations: 16,076,000,000 / 4,218,248,018,000 \u00d7 100 = 0.3811%; 16,400,000,000 / 4,434,356,468,000 \u00d7 100 = 0.3698%."
