    "chunk_size_bytes": 1886,
    "chunk_text": "Ministry of Women (LKR 16,400,000,000) as a share of this = 0.370% (\u2248 0.37%). Parliament of Sri Lanka\n\nThe Exact calculations: 16,076,000,000 / 4,218,248,018,000 \u00d7 100 = 0.3811%; 16,400,000,000 / 4,434,356,468,000 \u00d7 100 = 0.3698%.\n\nThe Manifesto A Thriving Nation, A Beautiful Life\u00a0 in it\u2019s Page 43 \u2013 Gender Equality / Impartial Human Identity states thus\n\nI quote \u201cAlthough women are an integral part of society, they consistently occupy an unequal position due to marginalization within major socioeconomic, cultural, and political systems. The NPP proposes a political practice that represents all marginalized groups in society, aiming to realize the aspirations of a just society, a free country, and free women by securing all rights.\n\nGender identities and sexual orientations are diverse. In Sri Lanka, these groups often face violence, marginalization, and stigmatization. Outdated colonial laws, institutional frameworks, and regressive cultural beliefs contribute to the denial of justice to these communities.\u201d\n\nHaving expressed your policy so eloquently the following principleshave been laid out; Economic justice as a cornerstone for achieving gender equality.State policies acknowledging the value of unpaid care work within the national economy. and Legislation that ensures fair and equal treatment for all marginalized groups.Further in page 5 under the title \u201cAn Empowered Woman you have promised to abolish all forms of gender discrimination, take measures,Take measures to relieve rural women from the burden of unfair microfinance loans and Initiate steps to address and end period poverty. Under social welfare schemes financial support for nutritious food supply during pregnancy and establishment of childcare centres at the Grama Niladhari (local) level have been promised\n\nIf we really summarize the pledges the NPP has promised the following:"
