    "md5": "23be5458afe9e09c6d667a9f15b58357",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1237,
    "chunk_text": "Having expressed your policy so eloquently the following principleshave been laid out; Economic justice as a cornerstone for achieving gender equality.State policies acknowledging the value of unpaid care work within the national economy. and Legislation that ensures fair and equal treatment for all marginalized groups.Further in page 5 under the title \u201cAn Empowered Woman you have promised to abolish all forms of gender discrimination, take measures,Take measures to relieve rural women from the burden of unfair microfinance loans and Initiate steps to address and end period poverty. Under social welfare schemes financial support for nutritious food supply during pregnancy and establishment of childcare centres at the Grama Niladhari (local) level have been promised\n\nIf we really summarize the pledges the NPP has promised the following:\n\nEconomic empowerment: They emphasize women\u2019s participation in the workforce, reducing barriers via childcare, financing, and training.\n\nSocial policy: NPP supports social infrastructure (e.g., childcare) to support women\u2019s labor participation.\n\nChild protection: They commit to community-based child safety, involving families, and systematic monitoring of child-wellbeing programs."
