    "md5": "51e7e1761ad880502ceb24e10248f161",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2024,
    "chunk_text": "Social policy: NPP supports social infrastructure (e.g., childcare) to support women\u2019s labor participation.\n\nChild protection: They commit to community-based child safety, involving families, and systematic monitoring of child-wellbeing programs.\n\nIn this document, while there are many policy areas, the gender-specific and children-specific commitments are not in a standalone \u201cwomen & children\u201d chapter; they are integrated under social policy / human rights / welfare.\n\n* Title: National People\u2019s Party (sic) Policy Framework \u2013 English (longer policy booklet) Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* This is more detailed and includes sections specifically on gender equality, women\u2019s rights, and children.\n\nThis is an analytical / interpretive document by a third party, not exactly the manifesto, but useful for understanding how NPP\u2019s policies on gender / children map onto broader discourse.\n\nHere are some of the relevant excerpts from the Policy Framework (from National People\u2019s Party Policy Framework \u2013 English):\n\nAdvancing Women\u2019s Rights and Economic Participation (Policy Framework, p. 62) Global Sri Lankan Congress+2Global Sri Lankan Congress+2\n\n* \u201cReview and amend all laws and policies that discriminate against women \u2026 in line with international human rights standards \u2026\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* \u201cEnact comprehensive legislation on gender equality \u2026 covering \u2026 employment, education, healthcare, property rights, and violence against women.\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* \u201cEstablish a National Commission on Women \u2026 to monitor the implementation of gender-responsive policies \u2026\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* \u201cImplement targeted programs \u2026 to support women\u2019s entrepreneurship, skills development \u2026 access to finance \u2026 particularly in high-growth and male-dominated sectors.\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* \u201cInvest in care infrastructure and services, such as childcare \u2026 to enable women\u2019s labor force participation \u2026\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress"
