    "chunk_text": "* \u201cImplement targeted programs \u2026 to support women\u2019s entrepreneurship, skills development \u2026 access to finance \u2026 particularly in high-growth and male-dominated sectors.\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* \u201cInvest in care infrastructure and services, such as childcare \u2026 to enable women\u2019s labor force participation \u2026\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\nChild Safety and Family Well-being (Policy Framework, p. 62) Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* \u201cCoordinate community organisations to ensure a coordinated approach to child safety.\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* \u201cEngage parents, families, and communities in the development and implementation of child safety initiatives.\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* \u201cSupport community-based programs \u2026 that promote child well-being and family stability.\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\n* \u201cRegularly assess and evaluate the effectiveness of child safety policies \u2026 making data-driven improvements as needed.\u201d Global Sri Lankan Congress\n\nIf you like, I can send you a link to download the exact English PDF of their manifesto that includes all gender-and-children-specific sections (or extract that as a plain-text \u201cwomen & children manifesto\u201d section). Do you want me to do that?\n\nGood question. Here is a link to the English version of the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) manifesto / policy document:\n\nA Thriving Nation \u2013 A Beautiful Life (NPP Manifesto, English PDF) muragala.lk\n\nIf you like, I can extract and send just the \u201cWomen & Children\u201d section (as text). Do you want me to do that?\n\nHere is an extracted version (in English) of key parts from the NPP (\u201cA Thriving Nation \u2013 A Beautiful Life\u201d) manifesto / policy statement that relate to women and children, with page references. (Based on the 2024 English manifesto PDF.) Muragala+1\n\nPage 43 \u2014 \u201cA\u202fThriving Nation \u201