    "chunk_text": "Here is an extracted version (in English) of key parts from the NPP (\u201cA Thriving Nation \u2013 A Beautiful Life\u201d) manifesto / policy statement that relate to women and children, with page references. (Based on the 2024 English manifesto PDF.) Muragala+1\n\nPage 43 \u2014 \u201cA\u202fThriving Nation \u2013 A Beautiful Life\u201d (Gender Equality / Impartial Human Identity)\n\nGender identities and sexual orientations are diverse. \u2026 in Sri Lanka, these groups often face violence, marginalization, and stigmatization. \u2026 outdated colonial laws, institutional frameworks, and regressive cultural beliefs contribute to the denial of justice to these communities.\n\n* Economic justice as a cornerstone for achieving gender equality. State policies acknowledging the value of unpaid care work within the national economy.\n\n* Legislation that ensures fair and equal treatment for all marginalized groups.\n\n* \u201cTake measures to relieve rural women from the burden of unfair microfinance loans.\u201d\n\nSocial Welfare Commitments (from analysis / summary of manifesto) \u2014 key promises relating to children:\n\n* Financial support for nutritious food packages during pregnancy and the first year of childbirth for lowincome families.\n\n* Establishment of childcare centers at the Grama Niladhari (local) level via public-private partnerships."
