    "chunk_text": "LowePublic presents NEQ, the podcast celebrating the Power of Unequal\n\nLowePublic, the Public Relations arm of the MullenLowe Group Sri Lanka, is expanding its reach in digital PR with the launch of NEQ \u2013 Not Equal To, a podcast curated to showcase professionals, brands and organisations who have performed extraordinarily by punching above their weight class and are not equal to others. Scheduled to debut across major social and streaming platforms in late November 2025, this initiative signals a bold evolution in how LowePublic connects with audiences through digital storytelling.\n\nHosted by Imran Saibo, the visionary founder of Funtime and a pioneer with over 30 years of expertise in bridging business and experience, NEQ unites distinct voices for conversations that challenge, provoke, and uncover perspectives that remain unseen in traditional media. Imran, a professional in economics and a pioneering figure in event marketing, will anchor the series, drawing out the essence of success from each guest, whether an individual, organisation or a brand that has redefined its category. Through sleek production, minimalist aesthetics, and sharp sound design, NEQ ventures beyond surface-level narratives to uncover the ideas, tensions, and legacies that shape not only remarkable individuals but also the visionary brands and enterprises transforming their worlds.\n\nCommenting on the launch, Lakshika Gunatilake, Head of Public Relations at LowePublic said, \u201cNEQ represents a natural progression for LowePublic as we expand our storytelling canvas beyond traditional PR. At its core, NEQ is about those who\u2019ve built, failed, led, and dared differently. We wanted to create a space where their stories could breathe without being edited down to soundbites. That\u2019s where real connection happens, and that\u2019s the heart of what we do at LowePublic.\u201d"
  },
