    "md5": "8a6d0b5102136b36e417192c60e71ed0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1696,
    "chunk_text": "A sensitive issue mismanaged\n\nThe Trincomalee temple issue has been grossly mismanaged. A tense situation arose when the Coast Conservation Department (CCD) objected to the construction of a building near Sri Sambuddha Jayanthi Bodhiraja Viharaya in Trincomalee on Sunday. A protest erupted when the police rushed in and forcibly took away a Buddha statue, which had been placed at the disputed site. Some protesters, including two Buddhist monks, were injured , according to media reports. The victims have complained of police assault.\n\nSri Lankan politicians seem to have a very low estimation of the intelligence of the public. Hence their numerous false claims and blatant lies for the consumption of the people, who vote for them. On listening to the government\u2019s absurd claim that the police had removed the Buddha statue in Trincomalee and kept it at a police station overnight because they wanted to ensure its safety, we were reminded of \u2018Matilda\u2019, whose \u201cdreadful lies made one gasp and stretch one\u2019s eyes\u201d. The statue had been returned to the temple the following morning, the government said. Going by the government\u2019s reasoning, one wonders how the police would have ensured the safety of a statue carved from a rock face, in case of threats of vandalism. There was absolutely no need for the police to remove the Buddha statue. They obviously overstepped their limits only to be asked by the government to return the statue in view of protests by the Opposition and Buddhist monks. They would not have resorted to force and removed the Buddha statue without the blessings of the political authority, which got cold feet due to the political fallout from the incident."
