    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan politicians seem to have a very low estimation of the intelligence of the public. Hence their numerous false claims and blatant lies for the consumption of the people, who vote for them. On listening to the government\u2019s absurd claim that the police had removed the Buddha statue in Trincomalee and kept it at a police station overnight because they wanted to ensure its safety, we were reminded of \u2018Matilda\u2019, whose \u201cdreadful lies made one gasp and stretch one\u2019s eyes\u201d. The statue had been returned to the temple the following morning, the government said. Going by the government\u2019s reasoning, one wonders how the police would have ensured the safety of a statue carved from a rock face, in case of threats of vandalism. There was absolutely no need for the police to remove the Buddha statue. They obviously overstepped their limits only to be asked by the government to return the statue in view of protests by the Opposition and Buddhist monks. They would not have resorted to force and removed the Buddha statue without the blessings of the political authority, which got cold feet due to the political fallout from the incident.\n\nThe angry reaction of the Illankai Tamil Arasu Kadchi (ITAK) to what it calls the lenient manner in which the government handled the construction at Bodhiraja Viharaya, and its call for all Tamil NPP MPs to pull out of the government in protest show that there is more to the issue than the alleged transgression of the coastal conservation laws. The ITAK has accused the NPP government of having capitulated to \u2018majoritarian forces\u2019. The devotees of Bodhiraja Viharaya insist that the building at issue is being constructed where a Dhamma school stood before the 2004 tsunami. They say they have documentary proof to support their claim. The CCD is apparently convinced otherwise."
