    "chunk_id": "2025-11-19-dbsjeyarajcom-b67f12fa-0008",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "4f4ed054f77134dd21fab0cf7b866842",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1878,
    "chunk_text": "In a controversial move, Gotabaya began pressuring his brother Mahinda to resign as Prime Minister to pave the way for a new premier. The other members of the Rajapaksa clan in government had all resigned earlier. Mahinda resisted the call to resign. But as the situation worsened and anti-Govt violence escalated,Mahinda submitted his resignation. This was immediately accepted by Gotabaya.\n\nThe gates were breached and mobs stormed in. An arson attack was launched. Around 20 Molotov Cocktails or Petrol bombs were thrown at the building. The fire was doused. Tear gas was fired repeatedly to disperse the mobs. Shots were fired in the air. Finally, Mahinda and Namal Rajapaksa with their families were evacuated by helicopter to the Trincomalee Naval Base. In a further development, the ancestral house of the Rajapaksas at Medamulana was attacked and destroyed. So too was the memorial dedicated to the parents of Chamal, Mahinda, Gotabaya and Basil.\n\nMuch water has flown under \u201cKelani Palama\u201dsince then.Gotabaya resigned and Ranil Wickremesinghe replaced him as President.Earlier Ranil had been appointed by Gota as oremier  after Mahinda\u2019s resignation. The Presidential elections of  September 2024 saw Anura Kumara Dissanayake becoming president. Parliamentary polls of November 2024 saw the JVP led NPP winning 159 seats and forming the Govt.\n\nThe  Rajapaksa family party the SLPP got three seats including one on the national list. The SLPP national list seat was given to Namal Rajapaksa  who is also the party\u2019s national organizer. He is the only member of the Medamulana Rajapaksa family currently  in Parliament. Namal tries hard to revive the party and bring about another Rajapaksa  political renaissance . Namal who finished a poor fourth at the 2024 Presidential poll, seems to have set his sights on gaining victory at the 2029 presidential elections."
