    "md5": "239bf0fbc47210d22969ef8b65c6da5a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2018,
    "chunk_text": "Her emotions touched their hearts \u2026and even made them cry\n\nTurning up at office last Monday (10) was none other than Noshin De Silva \u2013 the lead actress in the film \u2018Rayak Ho Payak.\u2019\n\nShe turned up with her mum and we chatted as if we have been friends for years! And \u2026 guess what?\n\nAlthough Noshin is Sri Lankan, by heritage, she was born and raised in Japan, until age 12, and then moved to the United States, where she completed middle school, high school, university, and her MBA in International Business.\n\nHer role in \u2018Rayak Ho Payak, \u2019 a thriller/suspense movie, is Aparna, a young mother facing the trauma of losing her child, and her acting has come in for high praise from those who have seen the movie.\n\nShe went on to say that many viewers mentioned to her that her portrayal of Aparna felt real and emotional.\n\n\u201cPeople said my emotions touched their hearts and even made them cry.\n\n\u201cThose comments mean the world to me. I feel rewarded as an actor when the audience can truly feel my emotions.\n\n\u201cSome people were surprised I could take on such a heavy, emotional role since I\u2019m usually a happy and bubbly person, but that\u2019s what I love most about acting \u2026 becoming someone completely different.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m deeply thankful to my mom, brother, director, and producers for believing in me.\u201d\n\nNoshin, indeed, is a bubbly person, and that was my first impression of her when we met.\n\nObviously, I needed to know how she got involved in this movie and she explained:\n\n\u201cI met the Director concerned while attending an acting workshop in Chennai, India, and after seeing me perform, he offered me the role of Aparna.\n\n\u201cBelieve me, I was instantly drawn to the character because the role required expressing deep emotions \u2013 sadness, panic, and unconditional love.\n\n\u201cThis was my first role with such emotional depth and intensity, and I was excited to challenge myself.\n\n\u201cI took the role seriously, studying how a mother might feel and react in such an unimaginable situation.\u201d"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
