    "chunk_size_bytes": 1898,
    "chunk_text": "Leading brands bag top awards at 11th CMA Sri Lanka Excellence in Integrated Reporting Awards 2025\n\nOverall winners: Bronze Award \u2013 Overall Second Runner-Up (Joint): Hayleys Fabric, LB Finance; Silver Award \u2013 Overall First Runner-Up (Joint): Commercial Bank, John Keells Holdings; Gold Award \u2013 Overall Winner (Joint): Softlogic Life Insurance, Talawakelle Tea Estates; Diamond Award \u2013 Overall Winner: Diesel & Motor Engineering\n\nThe Institute of Certified Management Accountants of Sri Lanka (CMA Sri Lanka) together with its Strategic Partner Colombo Stock Exchange successfully hosted the 11th Annual CMA Excellence in Integrated Reporting Awards 2025 on Monday, 17 November 2025, at the Hotel Cinnamon Life, The Forum.\n\nThe event celebrated outstanding achievements in corporate reporting and recognised organisations that have demonstrated leadership in transparency, accountability, and sustainable value creation beneficial to all stakeholders including employees, customers, suppliers, business partners, local communities, legislators, regulators and policy makers.\n\nThe Chief Guest was Labour Minister and Deputy Minister of Finance and Economic Development Prof. Anil Jayantha Fernando, Guest of Honour International Federation of Accountants President Jean Bouquot, Special Guest of Honour Former Supreme Court Judge of South Africa Prof. Mervyn King, Keynote Speaker and Chairman Panel of Judges Prof. Ho Yew Kee, Guest of Houour Colombo Stock Exchange CEO Rajeeva Bandaranayake together with CMA Sri Lanka President and CMA Excellence in Integrated Reporting Awards 2025 Chairman Prof. Lakshman R. Watawala.\n\nProf. Lakshman R. Watawala, Founder President of CMA Sri Lanka and Chairman of the CMA Excellence in Integrated Reporting Awards 2025, delivered the welcome address, emphasising the importance of integrated thinking in shaping resilient and future-ready organisations."
