    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Green-gram-purchasing-initiative-gets-Rs-764-m-boost/56-784586",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1763593336.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-11-20-dailyftlk-bd92e0ae-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "fa3d612da2371f4446174b45d6b80041",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1318,
    "chunk_text": "Green gram purchasing initiative gets Rs. 764 m boost\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers on Monday approved the allocation of funds to purchase the green gram harvest in competition with the private sector, further expanding the Government\u2019s existing procurement program.\n\nCabinet Spokesman and Minister Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa, addressing the weekly post-Cabinet media briefing yesterday said Rs. 764 million had been set aside for the initiative.\n\nUnder the 2025 Green Gram Crop Productivity and Production Enhancement Program, implemented in line with the guidelines of the Agriculture, Livestock, Land, and Irrigation Ministry, green gram was cultivated on around 16,500 hectares during the 2025 Yala and intermediate seasons. This cultivation was expected to yield around 14,600 tons, with roughly 12,000 tons anticipated to reach the local market.\n\nHarvesting had already begun in the Hambantota district, where reports indicated that middlemen were purchasing produce at a low price of Rs. 450 per kilogram.\n\n\u201cTo ensure that farmers received a fair price, the National Food Promotion Board, acting on the advice of the Ministry, began purchasing the green gram harvest directly from farmers,\u201d he said. The proposal to this effect was presented by Agriculture, Livestock, Land, and Irrigation Minister K.D. Lalkantha."
  },
