    "chunk_text": "He added that Sri Lanka is finalising a national registry, verification guidelines and project methodologies to meet global standards.\n\n\u201cOur aim is simple: every credit issued by Sri Lanka must be trusted and traceable. Once that trust is established, investment naturally follows, he said.\n\nPatabendi said nature-based solutions offer both ecological and economic returns.\n\n\u201cIf we restore degraded landscapes, we reduce disaster impacts, protect communities and open a new revenue stream. This is environmental protection with economic purpose, he noted.\n\n\u201cOur minerals cannot be exported as raw material indefinitely. We want a sector that is efficient, transparent and capable of generating higher value for the country while maintaining rigorous environmental standards, Patabendi said.\n\nLikuid Spaces at One Galle Face \u00a0redefining premium workspaces in Colombo\n\n\u2018Belavia Airlines flying to Sri Lanka augurs well for country\u2019s tourism\u2019\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
