    "md5": "19b9a76b3df0d353d23ef9c31c20c34b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1882,
    "chunk_text": "Restructuring of SriLankan Airlines\u2019 defaulted bonds has positive impact on CSE\n\nCSE trading overall was positive yesterday having experienced five days of decline. The change for the better came with a Singapore Stock Exchange announcement that SriLankan Airlines had restructured its defaulted bonds with a 15 percent haircut and other conditions.\n\n\u201cWe are very pleased to have finally reached an agreement with the Ad Hoc Group of Bondholders, allowing us to now look to the future of our company with greater optimism, chairman, SriLankan Airlines Sarath Ganegoda said in a CSE filing.\n\nMeanwhile, Treasury Secretary Harshana Suriyaperuma announced at a public event that SriLankan will complete the restructuring of 99 percent of its debt with the finalization of an agreement with holders of SriLankan Airlines defaulted bonds.\n\n\u201cToday we are taking a new step in the full normalization of our relations with our external partners and in our efforts to restore our public finances, he said in a filing on the Singapore Stock Exchange after reaching a deal to restructure SriLankan bonds.\n\nAmid those developments both indices moved upwards. The All Share Price Index went up by 75.10 points, while the S and P SL20 moved up by 25.02 points.\n\nTurnover stood at Rs 3.49 billion with ten crossings. Top seven crossings were reported in Commercial Bank, where 950,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 198 million; its shares traded at Rs 208.50, JKH 6.68 million shares crossed for Rs 152.3 million; its shares traded at Rs 22.80, VallibelOne 539,933 shares crossed for Rs 56.7 million; its shares traded at Rs 105, Cargills Bank 5.2 million shares crossed for Rs 55 million; its shares sold at Rs 105, Sunshine Holdings one million shares crossed for Rs 35 million; its shares traded at Rs 35 and CTC 15500 shares crossed for Rs 26.5 million and its shares fetched Rs 1700."
