    "md5": "ac7a0e5ca2b4490924fe25b4d003da70",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2007,
    "chunk_text": "Minister Jayatissa waxed eloquent on media ethics and the people\u2019s right to accurate information. He said the media must not publish anything based on unverified information, and faulted the aforesaid newspaper for having published the report at issue without ascertaining the views of the Ministry of Public Security and the Police. He also tore into a television station for having highlighted the news story. Let the newspaper and the television channel concerned engage in thrust and parry with the Media Minister; we intend to focus on the larger picture.\n\nWe are not short of self-righteous politicians. When Minister Jayatissa went ballistic yesterday, tearing into some journalists of print and electronic media, SJB MP Ajith P. Perera rose in defence of them. He said the Media Minister spoke as if \u2018possessed by Ranil Wickremesinghe\u2019, who had launched into tirades against senior journalists. Curiously, the NPP failed to point out that MP Perera had been a member of the UNP-led Yahapalana government when Wickremesinghe, as the Prime Minister, misused his parliamentary privileges to demonise some journalists. None of the SJB MPs, while they were in the  Yahapalana government, defended the media when Wickremesinghe berated journalists. Intoxicated with power, Wickremesinghe once went so far as to claim that the visage of a youthful presenter of the above-mentioned television station resembled that of \u2018Riri Yaka\u2019 or \u2018Demon of Blood\u2019! The Opposition MPs\u2019 defence of journalists and the government members\u2019 tirades against the independent media show the Jekyll-and-Hyde personality of politicians. Not all politicians are bad\u2014the good ones are either pushing up the daisies or out of power! It is popularly said in this country that \u2018bale thiyanakota mole ne, mole thiyanakota bale ne\u2019 (roughly rendered into English it means that \u2018when one has power, one has no brains; when one has brains, one has no power\u2019). The NPP leaders have exemplified this pithy saying."
