    "chunk_size_bytes": 807,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cEmotional abuse is often overlooked because there are no visible injuries. Victims may appear calm or compliant and abusers can present themselves as caring, making the signs difficult to detect. It\u2019s important to recognise warning indicators such as fearfulness, withdrawal, low self-confidence, avoiding eye contact, changes in mood, or minimising and excusing the abusive behaviour,\u201d\u00a0 De Silva noted.\n\nThis event formed part of Zonta\u2019s global \u201c16 Days of Activism\u201d campaign, inspired by the United Nations, aimed at ending violence against women in all its forms.\n\nThe program concluded with a powerful message: Although emotional abuse leaves no visible wounds, its scars run deep. Speaking up, seeking support and fostering awareness are the first steps toward healing and lasting change."
