    "chunk_size_bytes": 1829,
    "chunk_text": "SLBC to celebrate 35th anniversary with launch of inaugural SLBC EXPO Pavilion 2025\n\nOfficial opening today, 21 November at 2 p.m. at Pullman Dubai Creek City Centre\n\nThe Sri Lanka Business Council UAE (SLBC), under the Dubai Chamber of Commerce will begin its 35th Anniversary celebrations in 2026 with the launch of the inaugural SLBC EXPO Pavilion 2025, scheduled to be officially inaugurated today, 21 November at 2 p.m. at Pullman Dubai Creek City Centre.\n\nThe Chief Guest will be Ambassador of Sri Lanka to the UAE Prof. Arusha Cooray and Guests of Honour are SLBC Eminent Senior Adviser, Founder Member and Past Chairman Farook Kassim and Eminent Senior Adviser and Past Board Member Gamini Kannangara.\n\nSenior diplomats, corporate leaders, business councils, and members of the Sri Lankan community in the UAE will also be present.\n\nThe SLBC EXPO Pavilion 2025 will present a carefully curated selection of Sri Lankan excellence, featuring leading brands across diverse sectors. The participating brands are: Dilmah \u2013 premium Ceylon tea; China Harbour, Colombo Port City \u2013 real estate and investment hub; Prime Land \u2013 signature real estate developments; DFCC Bank \u2013 financial services and expatriate investment solutions; Deo Global Lanka \u2013 pure Ceylon cinnamon and spices; Sargia Holidays \u2013 bespoke travel and tourism experiences; Serendip Oud \u2013 authentic Ceylon oud; New Education Group \u2013 higher education and skill development; and Impact IT \u2013 technology and digital solutions.\n\nThe event is supported by Siraj Finance, Magic Mango, XESS Advertising, Pullman Creekside Deira City Centre (Official Hospitality Partner), Sri Lanka Bankers Association UAE and CASL UAE Chapter.\n\nThis powerful combination of exhibitors and supporters reflects the depth and diversity of Sri Lankan talent and enterprise."
