    "md5": "b518851e84a34d445f51fc77d8ac6de2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1930,
    "chunk_text": "The 2026 Budget reaffirms the government\u2019s commitment to improving living standards. It allocates Rs. 169 billion to ensure a decent and comfortable life for all citizens, Rs. 85.7 billion to expand access to safe drinking water, Rs. 13.5 billion for youth and sports initiatives, Rs. 19.6 billion for rural development, and Rs. 5.4 billion for urban infrastructure\u2014promoting balanced national growth.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s population distribution further underscores this approach: 77.4% reside in rural areas, 18.2% in urban centres, and 4.4% in the estate sector. This highlights the need for strong rural development policies, balanced regional planning, and targeted support for estate communities.\n\nThe digital economy is now central to modern growth, reshaping how value is created, traded, and scaled globally. Countries such as India, Vietnam, and South Korea demonstrate the transformative power of digital services, IT exports, and technology-driven manufacturing. By contrast, Sri Lanka\u2019s ICT sector remains underdeveloped, with limited digital penetration, SME adoption, and R&D investment. Promising areas include digital payments, the gig economy, AI, and analytics. Policies that strengthen digital infrastructure, promote tech innovation hubs, incentivize global tech investments, and build a digitally skilled workforce can position Sri Lanka as a regional digital leader.\n\nModern healthcare remains one of Sri Lanka\u2019s greatest national assets. Yet, rising non-communicable diseases, an ageing population, specialist shortages, and hospital overcrowding necessitate urgent modernization. Digital health offers transformative solutions: telemedicine, nationwide electronic health records, AI-assisted diagnostics, and regulated e-pharmacies. Scaling existing initiatives can enhance efficiency, equity, and outcomes, making quality healthcare accessible to all citizens, particularly in rural and estate sectors."
  },
