    "chunk_text": "Modern healthcare remains one of Sri Lanka\u2019s greatest national assets. Yet, rising non-communicable diseases, an ageing population, specialist shortages, and hospital overcrowding necessitate urgent modernization. Digital health offers transformative solutions: telemedicine, nationwide electronic health records, AI-assisted diagnostics, and regulated e-pharmacies. Scaling existing initiatives can enhance efficiency, equity, and outcomes, making quality healthcare accessible to all citizens, particularly in rural and estate sectors.\n\nWith political commitment, strategic investment, and integrated policy action, Sri Lanka can enter the next decade poised for a new economic renaissance\u2014equitable, resilient, and high-growth.\n\n*Visvalingam Muralithas is a researcher in the legislative sector, specializing in policy analysis and economic research. He is currently pursuing a PhD in Economics at the University of Colombo, with a research focus on governance, development, and sustainable growth."
