    "md5": "7e5b9110287c38afd025a6f9b3c3bb6d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1288,
    "chunk_text": "Aragalaya:Name the conspirators\n\nAragalaya (2022) is in the news again. Speaking at the launch of a book, Aragalaye Balaya authored by Dr. Sunanda Madduma Bandara, on Thursday, ex-President Ranil Wickremesinghe and former Speaker Mahinda Yapa Abeywardena reminisced about their experiences during the 2022 popular uprising and the subsequent wave of anarchical violence. Wickremesinghe denied having employed undemocratic methods to disperse Aragalaya protesters, and reiterated how democracy had been saved and the economy rebuilt.\n\nWhat was defeated was not Aragalaya as such. Aragalaya was a peaceful protest movement that emerged from people\u2019s legitimate grievances and resentment. Some sinister political forces moved in, following an SLPP goon attack on the GoGota Gama protesters at Galle Face in May 2022, and used Aragalaya as a launch pad for a violent campaign. It was those violent characters and their supporters who were attacked and stopped near Parliament. Minister K. D. Lal Kantha has admitted that the JVP tried to capture Parliament but its efforts came a cropper. The SLPP government went on to disperse the  Aragalaya protesters at Galle Face. However, the JVP effectively tapped into public anger and rode to power on the crest of a massive wave of anti-politics."
  },
