    "chunk_size_bytes": 1637,
    "chunk_text": "What was defeated was not Aragalaya as such. Aragalaya was a peaceful protest movement that emerged from people\u2019s legitimate grievances and resentment. Some sinister political forces moved in, following an SLPP goon attack on the GoGota Gama protesters at Galle Face in May 2022, and used Aragalaya as a launch pad for a violent campaign. It was those violent characters and their supporters who were attacked and stopped near Parliament. Minister K. D. Lal Kantha has admitted that the JVP tried to capture Parliament but its efforts came a cropper. The SLPP government went on to disperse the  Aragalaya protesters at Galle Face. However, the JVP effectively tapped into public anger and rode to power on the crest of a massive wave of anti-politics.\n\nAbeywardena\u2019s statement has confirmed what ousted President Gotabaya Rajapaksa and National Freedom Front Leader Wimal Weerawansa have said in their books on the 2022 uprising, its causes and fallout\u2014The Conspiracy, and Nine: The Hidden Story, respectively. It has lent credence to the conspiracy theories about the 2022 uprising. Gotabaya has said in his book that his ouster in 2022 was due to an internationally-backed conspiracy. Weerawansa has argued that there was a foreign involvement in Aragalaya and accused the US of having used Aragalaya to compass its geopolitical ends. He was the first to reveal that some foreign governments had tried to railroad Speaker Abeywardena into taking over the presidency. His critics sought to dismiss his claim as a figment of his imagination. The US embassy in Colombo denied his claim at issue, calling his book a work of fiction."
