    "chunk_size_bytes": 1932,
    "chunk_text": "Nufloe elevates movement and rehabilitation in Sri Lanka through Pilates\n\nLocated in the heart of Colombo, Nufloe is changing how Sri Lankans move, recover, and reconnect with their bodies through Pilates. Established in 2025, Nufloe is the country\u2019s first fully equipped Balanced Body\u00ae Pilates studio, setting a new standard in mindful movement, rehabilitation, and boutique fitness. Behind its serene Japandi-inspired interiors and the calm rhythm of curated playlists lies a purpose-driven philosophy to create a space where movement meets medicine, and where every individual, regardless of age or ability, can find strength through movement.\n\nNufloe is the only Pilates studio in Sri Lanka to offer the full range of Balanced Body\u00ae equipment, including the Reformer, Cadillac Trapeze Table, Tower, EXO Chair, Combo Chair, and Spinefitter. This allows clients to experience the same professional-grade quality found in leading studios worldwide. Each piece of apparatus is designed to improve flexibility, strength, and balance while ensuring every session remains low-impact and gentle on the joints. Whether you\u2019re new to Pilates or an experienced mover, each class, whether group, private, or beginner, provides a guided journey towards better posture, deeper core strength, and greater mobility.\n\nSavindya Tissera, founder of Nufloe and professionally trained under the Balanced Body\u00ae Pilates teacher training, hails from a corporate background, specialising in strategy and corporate finance. Having been a Pilates practitioner for over 10 years, she believes Pilates is more than a form of exercise; it\u2019s a tool for lifelong health.\n\nSri Lanka College of Endocrinologists and Morison continue commitment to diabetes care\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
