    "chunk_size_bytes": 1925,
    "chunk_text": "The Election Commission (EC) has reportedly said a fresh delimitation process will take about one year to reach completion. A PSC can be made to drag on, delaying the PC polls indefinitely. This seems to be the NPP\u2019s battle plan. It is said that when a government fears the people, there is liberty. But when a government fears elections, democracy is in jeopardy. Since 2017, three governments have kept the PC polls in limbo by refusing to take action to hold them.\n\nIronically, some election monitors have urged the NPP government either to hold the PC polls expeditiously or to decide whether to retain the PCs, as it is antithetical to democracy to allow the PCs to be kept under the President through the Provincial Governors appointed by him. An opportunity has now presented itself for the JVP to fulfil its vow to do away with the PC system. The JVP drove thousands of its cadres to take up arms and lay down their lives in the name of a campaign to scuttle the PC system, among others, in the late 1980s The JVP leaders were seen recently commemorating the party members killed during their abortive uprising. They have made an about-turn on that vow, and are all out to retain control of the PCs by postponing elections further.\n\nThe Opposition is pretending that its leaders and members had nothing to do with the postponement of the PC polls. But they helped the  Yahapalana government amend the PC Elections Act in 2017 to put off elections on the pretext of increasing female representation in the PCs. Most of the SJB MPs who were in the UNP at the time, the JVP, those who are in the SLPP at present, the SLMC, the TNA, etc., facilitated the passage of an amendment bill, which was changed beyond recognition at the committee stage, with a slew of sections smuggled into it to pave the way for the postponement of the PC polls as the UNP-led Yahapalana government was scared of facing an electoral contest."
