    "chunk_size_bytes": 1748,
    "chunk_text": "Sex Education in Schools\n\nI have been reading opinions about the introduction of an overhauled system of education in schools next year. One of the controversial issues was closing of primary schools in rural areas due to low attendance in these schools; another being sex education to be included in the syllabus for Grade six kids, usually aged around 11 years.\n\nPity schools are being closed in rural areas with total attendance less than a hundred and paucity of teachers, often one managing and teaching all the students. An impossible task. But due to economic reasons and others like lack of adults to escort the kids to larger schools situated in towns nearby, many a child is deprived of education. Hence the suggestion that although schools with low attendance are closed down, affected children will be taken to a school and back home with the government providing buses and escorts.\n\nA more controversial and generalized question is compulsory sex education for pre-puberty Grade six students. Archbishop Malcolm Cardinal Ranjith recently preached a sermon expressing his views on the subject and the view of the Roman Catholic Church, if not all Christians. The contents were reported in this newspaper. He brought in the opinion that the proposed sex education syllabus included deviant sexual preferences as blanketed by the term LGBTQ+. The acronym stands for the ever increasing group of lesbians, gay, bi and transsexuals, queers and others who are different from bisexual people. They are now quite a powerful lobby with their many hued flag. The Cardinal feared these persons would be accepted as equal to \u2018normal\u2019 sexually oriented men and women. A new gender is also being created to add to feminine and masculine genders."
