    "chunk_text": "A more controversial and generalized question is compulsory sex education for pre-puberty Grade six students. Archbishop Malcolm Cardinal Ranjith recently preached a sermon expressing his views on the subject and the view of the Roman Catholic Church, if not all Christians. The contents were reported in this newspaper. He brought in the opinion that the proposed sex education syllabus included deviant sexual preferences as blanketed by the term LGBTQ+. The acronym stands for the ever increasing group of lesbians, gay, bi and transsexuals, queers and others who are different from bisexual people. They are now quite a powerful lobby with their many hued flag. The Cardinal feared these persons would be accepted as equal to \u2018normal\u2019 sexually oriented men and women. A new gender is also being created to add to feminine and masculine genders.\n\nHaving been in a school hostel in Kandy from Grade six onward, admiring teachers, even senior students, was a common feature. There was nothing sexual in this, purely platonic. Girls were usually happy in school hostels, but being separated from the togetherness of family life, one tended to miss the warmth of a mother\u2019s care and concern. Hence unknowingly, emotional satisfaction was sought from admiring someone older. We named it \u2018running after\u2019 but it was harmless.\n\nMore serious attachments were sometimes forged with hostel mates. There was the desire to be close to a friend, sleep with her if possible and some sort of special love grew. A bit of fondling would also arise. But this was all a passing phase and not to be cautious about. Once in a while it was serious and one or both partners would develop homosexual preferences; boys were irrelevant to them, even disliked."
