    "chunk_text": "To come to the point of this article which is my opinion on sex education in schools. As a writer of a letter to the editor recently opined it is more urgent and relevant to impart information on drug abuse and prevention to school kids. Drug use is rampant in schools and getting graver. Knowing about dangerous drugs is much more important and urgent than deviant sex. But I say sex education is important and necessary: what evils prevail; how a child can be aware of sex predators and avoid them; how to act if approached and what help is available. The two issues can be included in the school syllabus but probably for Grade seven and above.\n\nThus sex education should be introduced to schools but in a mild way, casually almost. No song and dance made about it, with greater emphasis on drug abuse.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
