    "chunk_size_bytes": 1986,
    "chunk_text": "LTL Transformers secures $2.6 Mn export order to Mauritius\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s LTL Transformers Private Limited has secured a major export order of 350 high-efficiency Amorphous Transformers to the State of Mauritius, valued at over USD 2.6 million, highlighting the country\u2019s engineering expertise on a global scale.\n\nThe order, awarded through an International Competitive Bidding (ICB) process by the Central Electricity Board of Mauritius, saw LTL Transformers outperform leading international manufacturers. The formal handover ceremony for the shipment was held yesterday at the company\u2019s facility.\n\nThe transformers were verified through independent factory inspections and Factory Acceptance Tests (FAT) to meet IEC standards and the technical requirements of Mauritius\u2019 electricity board.\n\nSpeaking at the event, LTL Transformers CEO Rukki Patberiya noted that the company has installed more than 16,000 transformers across Sri Lanka, generating millions in revenue. The 350 transformers will be shipped in phases, with a total of 750 units destined for Mauritius.\n\nAmorphous-core transformers reduce no-load losses, minimize energy wastage, improve efficiency, and lower the carbon footprint, representing a significant step toward sustainable power generation. LTL Transformers\u2019 facility adheres to international standards in design, engineering, manufacturing, and testing, strengthening its position as a reliable global supplier.\n\nThis milestone not only boosts Sri Lanka\u2019s economy but also showcases the skill and capability of Sri Lankan engineers across Africa, Asia, and the Middle East.\n\nComBank and Abans forge landmark partnership with POS and digital payments rollout\n\nHNB FINANCE Posts Rs. 620 Mn PAT, Up by 129% Year-on-Year during the First Half of the FY 2025/26\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
