    "md5": "f70e93ba0e7bdcb2f543547ddea93377",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1786,
    "chunk_text": "Sybil Wettasinghe\u2019s magic of storytelling continues\n\nBook Launch: The Magic Silver Tree and Sybil Wettasinghe\u2019s latest books, The Magic Silver Tree and Puduma Ridi Gaha, posthumously published by Adith Publishers, will be launched on the 24 November 2025, at 3.30pm at the Lionel Wendt Art Centre, Colombo. Exhibition of the original artwork from the books will continue on the 25th November, from 9.30am to 7.30pm.\n\nand Puduma Ridi Gaha, based on a mythical folk story, continues Sybil Wettasinghe\u2019s legacy of enchanting narratives through words and pictures, weaving together her timeless art of storytelling with endearingly beautiful and lively illustrations. First published in Japan in 2017, the artwork of The Magic Silver Tree has been recognized as one the finest illustrations done by Sybil Wettasinghe.\n\nIn her career spanning over 70 years, Sybil Wettasinghe wrote and illustrated over 400 books, and won eight state literary awards and several international awards, including the prestigious Nikkei Award from Japan in 2012. Her iconic book Kuda Hora has been translated into eight languages. The Magic Silver Tree is the last of her books to be published in Japan during her lifetime, with seven other books preceding this including favourite titles such as Hoity the Fox, Runaway Beard, Visitors to the Cat Country, Dancing in the Gourd, and the translation of her autobiography, The Child in Me.\n\nThe launch of The Magic Silver Tree and Puduma Ridi Gaha and the exhibition, celebrating Sybil\u2019s unique style of storytelling and illustrations, are open to the public from 24th to 25th November, 2025.\n\nSybil Wettasinghe (October 31, 1928 \u2013 June 30, 2020) was a pioneering figure in Sri Lankan children\u2019s literature, whose work continues to inspire generations."
  },
