    "md5": "0583115c3d70692f693c6efc39e05a58",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1097,
    "chunk_text": "In total, Sybil Wettasinghe authored and illustrated over 400 children\u2019s books, in addition to illustrating hundreds more for other authors. Eight of her books were published in Japan, the last being Magic Silver Tree. She wrote in both Sinhala and English, with many of her work being translated into Tamil.\n\nSybil passed away peacefully on June 30, 2020, leaving behind an enduring literary and artistic legacy.\n\nSybil\u2019s youngest son, Vinod Wettasinghe, worked meticulously on the layout and design to ensure that the quality of his mother\u2019s artistry was preserved. After months of dedicated effort, he published the book through his family company, Adith Publishers (Pvt) Ltd., the principal publisher of Sybil\u2019s works.\n\nThe Magic Silver Tree is a hardcover edition with silver-embossed detailing, making it a treasured collector\u2019s item or a meaningful gift for readers and art lovers alike.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
