    "chunk_text": "Despite such differences, Americans read British books and newspapers without difficulty. Similarly, those who have studied British English can easily understand American books, magazines, films and songs. The barriers between British English and American English are breaking down.\n\nAs the student population is exposed to American English through the use of the Internet and mobile phones, they have to be educated about the British spelling rules and expressions. If the authorities fail to educate them properly, future generations will use a hotchpotch of British English and American English.\n\nHow Lee Kuan Yew turned a small island into a global powerhouse\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
