    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "Prime Lands Residencies\u2019 success story is shared by over 7,200 Sri Lankan investors\n\nThe remarkable financial turnaround of Prime Lands Residencies PLC (PLR) is more than a corporate success story; it is a direct financial victory for a broad cross-section of the Sri Lankan public. With a wide public ownership base of over 7,200 investors on the Colombo Stock Exchange, the company\u2019s soaring performance has directly increased the wealth and solidified the investments of thousands of ordinary citizens.\n\nThis period of shared prosperity is underscored by the company\u2019s formidable financial foundation, which now boasts a Shareholder Equity of Rs. 10.3 billion. This equity signals not just corporate resilience but also the security of the public\u2019s investment, supporting a market capitalization of LKR 31.9 billion.\n\nThe most visible sign of this success for PLR\u2019s vast investor community has been the dramatic rally in its share price, which more than doubled to close at Rs. 34.20. This surge is fundamentally rooted in performance that delivers tangible value to its owners. The key metric for these shareholders, Earnings Per Share (EPS), surged by 72% to LKR 0.58, proving that the company\u2019s growth is directly enriching its large and diverse public base.\n\nBehind this shareholder value is operational excellence. While revenue grew 24% to Rs. 2.84 billion, the real achievement was in profitability, with Gross Profit up 52% and Profit Before Tax accelerating by 74%. This disciplined growth means the company is not just expanding, but creating more value for its thousands of stakeholders.\n\nCompany leadership affirmed that this performance is a validation of a strategy designed to build lasting value."
