    "md5": "fbc6d4e14aad6bc9c6fbf28c74864bf8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1569,
    "chunk_text": "Union Assurance report exposes silent Diabetes crisis in Sri Lanka\n\nUnion Assurance\u2019s \u2018Suwamaga Impact Report,\u2019 reviewing 15 months of its flagship CSR initiative, reveals critical insights into Sri Lanka\u2019s diabetes epidemic. The nationwide programme provided free screenings to over 23,000 individuals across all 25 districts, surpassing its goal by 155%.\n\nThe data uncovers a severe health crisis. Among those flagged for advanced HbA1c testing, 76% were diagnosed with diabetes. Alarmingly, nearly 3% of all beneficiaries learned they had diabetes for the first time through this initiative.\n\nBeyond diagnosis, the programme drove tangible behavioural change, with 71% of beneficiaries adopting healthier lifestyles. The initiative, featuring a mobile screening unit with healthcare professionals, provided critical early detection and risk management.\n\n\u201cThis report underscores the urgent need for collective action,\u201d said CEO Senath Jayatilake. \u201cWe have demonstrated significant impact and call on all stakeholders to join us in strengthening national prevention strategies.\u201d\n\nUnion Assurance remains committed to expanding this vital work, empowering Sri Lankans to protect their health and future.\n\nTVS Lanka empowers 210 garage mechanics with free NVQ certifications\n\nRoyal Palms Beach recognised for \u2018exceptional sustainability\u2019 at NCP Awards 2025\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
