    "chunk_size_bytes": 1816,
    "chunk_text": "TVS Lanka empowers 210 garage mechanics with free NVQ certifications\n\nIn a significant boost for Sri Lanka\u2019s automotive sector, TVS Lanka certified 210 Private Garage Mechanics (PGMs) with NVQ Level 4 qualifications at a ceremony held at the BMICH on October 29.\n\nThe technicians received their certifications free of charge through the TVS Knowledge Centre, the country\u2019s only private institute officially recognized by the government to offer NVQ Level 4 certification for motorcycle technicians in collaboration with NAITA and the Tertiary and Vocational Education Commission (TVEC).\n\nThis initiative marks a major milestone in public-private partnerships for vocational training, directly addressing the need for standardized, high-quality skills development within the two-wheeler industry.\n\n\u201cTVS is delighted to contribute to transforming the country\u2019s most valuable asset- its human resources,\u201d said Geethal Anthony, CEO of TVS Lanka. He emphasized the Centre\u2019s role as a catalyst for upskilling aspiring technicians for a modernized mobility landscape.\n\nThe company highlighted that providing this advanced training and certification at no cost is a core part of its mission to uplift the Sri Lankan automobile workforce, enabling them to compete globally.\n\nThe landmark event was attended by Chief Guest G. Srinivasan Raghavan, Director of TVS Lanka and Chairman & Managing Director of TVS Mobility Pvt. Ltd, India, alongside other dignitaries.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s Halal Council recognised for quality as certified exports hit $1.9 billion\n\nUnion Assurance report exposes silent Diabetes crisis in Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
