    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s Halal Council recognised for quality as certified exports hit $1.9 billion\n\nThe Halal Assessment Council (HAC) received a Merit Award at the prestigious Sri Lanka National Quality Awards 2023.\n\nThe award recognizes HAC\u2019s commitment to upholding international certification standards, which help Sri Lankan producers access global markets and build consumer trust. This trusted certification is a major economic driver.\n\nIn 2024, Sri Lanka\u2019s exports of Halal-certified products were estimated at USD 1.9 billion. This accounts for 63 percent of all food and beverage exports and 16 percent of the nation\u2019s total exports, underscoring the critical role of certification in the country\u2019s export economy.\n\nIIHS opens doors to global healthcare careers with new intake for five flagship programmes\n\nTVS Lanka empowers 210 garage mechanics with free NVQ certifications\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
