    "md5": "4ebce99fe972ac29b012d1acd6b4f4e9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1809,
    "chunk_text": "Teachers wave cane at govt.\n\nTrade unions representing school teachers and principals have resolved to launch a countrywide strike on 12 December. They accuse the NPP government of continuing to ignore their problems and trying to railroad them into accepting its educational reforms, which they have rejected as ill-conceived. The school system is already grappling with various delays, and a strike by teachers and principals will make an already bad situation far worse. But the government does not seem to care. It bellows rhetoric, casts aspersions on all who express dissent, and bulldozes its way through, apparently in the belief that its mandate has come not from the people but from another dimension. We have seen such juggernauts careen downhill, spiral out of control, crash and shatter into pieces.\n\nState workers, especially teachers and principals, played a very active role in bringing the NPP to power, last year, as evident from the massive swing in the postal votes for it. The government has kicked away the ladder and antagonised many trade unions. Kalutara District United Teachers\u2019 Union Secretary, Tharindu Dilshan, has said teachers now regret ever having campaigned and voted for the NPP! General Secretary of the Ceylon Teachers\u2019 Union Joseph Stalin has claimed that even the JVP\u2019s Ceylon Teachers Service Union, once led by Deputy Minister Mahinda Jayasinghe, has closed ranks with the protesting trade unions. The governments of self-proclaimed leftists are no different from the capitalist regimes in their handling of labour disputes; they, too, ride roughshod over trade unions after winning elections with the help of workers. One may recall how the United Front government, comprising leftists, especially the LSSP, broke a bank employees\u2019 strike in the early 1970s."
  },
