    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "08221fbf1645aa3a79654a7c56a054e9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1960,
    "chunk_text": "Macksons Solar sets new benchmark with largest rooftop installation\n\nIndustries and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunneththi (centre) along with Macktiles Lanka Managing Director Mizver Makeen (right) and Macksons Holdings Chairman Milfer Makeen (extreme left) at the unveiling ceremony\n\nIn a landmark move for Sri Lanka\u2019s renewable energy sector, Macksons Solar, in collaboration with Macktiles, unveiled the country\u2019s largest rooftop solar project at the Macktiles Lanka Ltd., factory complex in Bandaragama.\n\nThis 10 megawatt (MW) installation comprises over 18,000 high efficiency solar panels, advanced inverter systems and state-of-the-art monitoring technology.\n\nTogether, they are expected to generate approximately 12 GWh of clean energy annually, while reducing approximately 8,000 tonnes of carbon emissions each year.\n\nSpread across the extensive rooftop of the Macktiles manufacturing facility, the 10 MW solar system delivers renewable energy directly to the plant, significantly lowering its reliance on grid power while channelling surplus electricity to support a more sustainable national energy network.\n\nMacksons Solar CEO Sajjaad Saliheen said: \u201cThis project is not just about size - it\u2019s about vision, innovation and responsibility. We are proud to partner with Macktiles in leading Sri Lanka\u2019s transition toward renewable energy. This 10 MW installation demonstrates how large-scale industries can embrace sustainability without compromising productivity or profitability.\u201d\n\nThe official unveiling ceremony was graced by several distinguished guests, including Industries and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunneththi as Chief Guest, along with Labour Minister and Finance and Planning Deputy Minister Dr. Anil Jayantha Fernando, Energy Deputy Minister M.I.M. Arkam, Kalutara District Member of Parliament Nandana Padmakumara and Millaniya Pradeshiya Sabha Vice Chairperson Jayasena Rodrigue."
  },
