    "md5": "82da8bcf29da4794ba3a35b363d0ba5c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1596,
    "chunk_text": "The official unveiling ceremony was graced by several distinguished guests, including Industries and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunneththi as Chief Guest, along with Labour Minister and Finance and Planning Deputy Minister Dr. Anil Jayantha Fernando, Energy Deputy Minister M.I.M. Arkam, Kalutara District Member of Parliament Nandana Padmakumara and Millaniya Pradeshiya Sabha Vice Chairperson Jayasena Rodrigue.\n\nMacktiles continues to set benchmarks in sustainable manufacturing through initiatives like this, reinforcing its commitment to environmental responsibility.\n\nMacktiles Lanka Managing Director Mizver Makeen said: \u201cAt Macktiles, we believe progress and sustainability must go hand in hand. This 10 MW solar project is a testament to our commitment to responsible growth and clean energy. Partnering with Macksons Solar enables us to set a benchmark for the manufacturing sector in Sri Lanka.\u201d\n\nDemonstrating the strength of Sri Lankan expertise, Macksons Solar\u2019s in-house technical team led the full design, engineering, and commissioning of the project- a testament to the company\u2019s ability to deliver renewable energy infrastructure of international standards.\n\nWith this milestone, Macksons Solar strengthens its position as a leader in Sri Lanka\u2019s solar industry, supporting the country\u2019s target of achieving 70% renewable energy by 2030.\n\n\u201cThis 10-MW project represents what\u2019s possible when innovation meets commitment. It\u2019s a proud moment for both our teams- and a major leap towards a greener, energy-secure Sri Lanka,\u201d added Saliheen."
  },
