    "chunk_text": "Lankem Ceylon buys majority stake in York Arcade for Rs. 340.58 m\n\nLankem Ceylon PLC yesterday acquired a 49.27% stake in York Arcade Holdings PLC from its parent company, The Colombo Fort Land and Building PLC, in a transaction valued at Rs. 340.58 million.\n\nThe deal, involving 369,495 ordinary voting shares at Rs. 921.75 per share, was executed on the trading floor of the Colombo Stock Exchange.\n\nLankem said the acquisition supports the Group\u2019s ongoing financial restructuring efforts.\n\nThe company noted that consolidating ownership in York Arcade is part of a broader plan to strengthen the group\u2019s balance sheet and operational alignment.\n\nYork Arcade closed at. 892.50 yesterday, down from the previous close of Rs. 921.75. The company reported a Rs. 304.21 net asset per share as of end September 2025. At that date, Colombo Fort Land and Building PLC was the majority shareholder at 49.27%."
