    "md5": "458b8e8340ca6a08538e275fa179ad9c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1989,
    "chunk_text": "Most of all, there is nothing criminal about the newspaper reports on the PSCs and police clearance certificates. It therefore defies comprehension why the CID has been called in to conduct an investigation. The government is obviously trying to intimidate the media, control information and suppress dissent.\n\nThe JVP has been accused of infiltrating all community organisations. The Opposition\u2019s argument that the JVP is all out to use these outfits to consolidate its power at the grassroots level is tenable. The move to make PSC recommendations mandatory for the issuance of police reports is seen as part of the JVP\u2019s strategy.\n\nThe CID seems to have forgotten that there are far more important things it has to intensify its focus on, the Easter Sunday carnage being a case in point. Minister Jayatissa never misses an opportunity to pontificate to the media on journalistic ethics. He often urges journalists to get their facts right. So, there is reason to believe that he followed the aforesaid ethical guidelines when he made a statement about the mastermind behind the Easter Sunday terror attacks. He was a member of the Parliamentary Select Committee that probed the Eastern Sunday carnage in 2019. When he was in the Opposition, four years ago, he told BBC that according to \u2018investigative evidence\u2019 he was privy to, India had been behind the terror attacks. He is now the Cabinet Spokesman. It will be interesting to know the other government leaders\u2019 position on his allegation. Curiously, the CID has not recorded a statement from him on this very serious claim. Doesn\u2019t the CID consider information about the mastermind behind the Easter Sunday carnage far more serious than a newspaper report about police reports?\n\nThe CID would do well to get its priorities right, without going out of its way to advance the government\u2019s political agenda.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *"
