    "chunk_text": "HNB becomes Platinum sponsor of TiECON 2026 to power Sri Lanka\u2019s runway to the world\n\nhanding over the sponsorship to TiE Colombo President Madu Ratnayake. HNB Chief Operating Officer Sanjay Wijemanne and TiE Colombo Vice President Dinesh Saparamadu (extreme right) are also present\n\nHNB PLC has been announced as the Platinum Sponsor of TiECON Colombo 2026 which will take place in early 2026 in Colombo. Organised by TiE Colombo, the event serves as Sri Lanka\u2019s premier platform for innovation and entrepreneurship, bringing together entrepreneurs, intrapreneurs, investors, and global business leaders. It features keynotes, panel discussions, networking opportunities, investor lounges, and an innovation showcase, creating a comprehensive forum for knowledge exchange and business growth.\n\nHNB MD/CEO Damith Pallewatte said, \u201cAs Sri Lanka\u2019s Partner in Progress, HNB has always stood beside the businesses that drive national transformation. Our partnership with TiECON Colombo 2026 is both timely and strategic, we believe the future of Sri Lankan enterprise lies in going global. Together with TiE Colombo, we aim to fuel that journey, giving local entrepreneurs the networks, financial tools, and confidence they need to take off and thrive on the world runway.\u201d\n\nThis year\u2019s theme \u201cGo Global Runway to the World marks\u201d a decisive stage for the local business community as enterprises prepare to shift from resilience led recovery toward opportunity driven expansion. HNB\u2019s role as Platinum Sponsor aligns with its position as the first and the best in Sri Lanka\u2019s banking sector with a legacy of enabling business advancement and national progress.\n\nTiE Colombo President Madu Ratnayake said, \u201cTiECON 2026 is not just another conference. It\u2019s a launchpad. With HNB as our Platinum sponsor, we\u2019re strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s runway to the world, connecting our most promising founders to the people, ideas, and capital that can help them soar globally.\u201d"
